21234      ods path work.templat(update) sashelp.tmplmst(read);
21235      
21236      data Children;
21237      input ID City$ @@;
21238      do i=1 to 4;
21239      input Age Smoke Symptom @@;
21240      output;
21241      end;
21242      datalines;

NOTE: SAS went to a new line when INPUT statement reached past the end of a line.
NOTE: The data set WORK.CHILDREN has 100 observations and 6 variables.

21268      ;
21269      proc gee data=Children descending;
21270      class ID City;
21271      model Symptom = City Age Smoke / dist=bin link=logit;
21272      repeated subject=ID / type=exch covb corrw;
21273      run;

NOTE: PROC GEE is modeling the probability that Symptom='1'.
NOTE: The PROCEDURE GEE printed page 2359.

